    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nREA Donohoe Spring are delighted to present to the market this Characterful 2 Bed Bungalow with Detached Garage on Enclosed C. 0.35 Acre Site. Recently Renovated with Some Minor Works Cosmetic Touches Remaining. Peaceful Location with Panoramic Views, C. 8.6 km to Amenities. For Sale By Private Treaty with fixtures, fittings appliances. \n\nThis stone built bungalow has been recently renovated throughout with living accommodation extending to C. 105 sqm/1,120 sqft comprising;\n\nPorch (2.2. x 1.4), Hallway (2.5 x 1.4), Rear study hall (3.3 x 1.4) with glass door to garden, Spacious Kitchen/Diner (5.4 x 4.4) with handmade kitchen range cooker, Sitting Room (5.5 x 4.1) with solid fuel stove, Lobby (2.7 x 1.5),\n\nBedroom 1 (4.2 x 3.6), Shower Room (2.7 x 2.5) and Bedroom 2 (4.2 x 2.7).\n\nA Stira stair from the Lobby accesses an attic room (4.2 x 2.7) providing additional living space an option for a 3rd bedroom. There is also an externally accessed Utility room (1.9 x 1.9) to rear of residence.\n\n \n\nThe original stone schoolhouse dates back to C. 1900 and was extended to the side with block construction. The recent renovation works include; Installation of uPVC double glazed windows doors throughout, New roof structure with original tiles retained, Re-wired throughout, Re-plumbed including installation of a new oil boiler, new high efficiency hot water tank pressurised water system, Handmade Kitchen with all new appliances including a range cooker. For sale with fixtures, fittings appliances.\n\n \n\nThere are some minor works required to fully complete with costings available for same. Those seeking more space can extend up to 45 sqm to the rear, exempt from planning permission.\n\n \n\nThe singular property retains many original features including high ceilings (3.7m) in the Kitchen/Diner Sitting room. Other features include; Built-in-storage and shelving in the Porch Sitting room, Eaves storage space in the Bonus room, Ample plug sockets throughout including external weather-proof sockets, Built-in closets in both bedrooms Large picture windows in all front facing rooms to maximise views.\n\n \n\nServiced by: Corlough Group Water Scheme Connection, Septic tank waste treatment system and Oil fired central heating with a new boiler. Fibre broadband is available. BER: G (Pre-renovation assessment).\n\n \n\nThe property occupies a level roadside site of C. 0.35 acres with defining boundary wall. A stone driveway provides ample off-street parking the detached garage (3.9 x 5.8) ha mezzanine storage space. To the side and rear is a generous lawn area with patio and seating areas, wood trellis style gazebo attached to rear of the residence and even a slate roof bar (1.6 x 2.3) entertaining space.\n\n \n\nA superb bungalow with real character in a beautiful setting. A perfect home, holiday home or rental investment offering excellent potential in the right hands.\n\n \n\nSituated in the Unesco Cuilcagh Lakelands Geopark, along the R200 in a scenic rural location 8.5km to amenities in Swanlinbar. C. 15 min drive to Ballyconnell and approx. 30 min to a wide range of amenities in Enniskillen 40 mins to Cavan Town. Convenient to Brackley Amenities, Cuilcagh Boardwalk, Shannon Pot Shannon-Erne Blue. GPS: 54.157722, -7.770232. \n\n \n\nViewing Highly Recommended by Appointment Only. \n\n"
      }
    ],
